        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "891dcb96-2e02-577e-a32e-e44024a9cd66",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: James B. Donovan, Francis Gary Powers, Rudolf Abel, Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher\n- Organizations: U.S. Air Force, Soviet KGB\n- Places: Soviet Union, United States\n- Events: Cold War, 1960 U-2 incident, spy exchange, Rudolf Abel trial\n- Works: Bridge of Spies\n\nFacts:\n- Rudolf Ivanovich Abel, whose real name was Vilyam \"Willie\" Genrikhovich Fisher, was born on July 11, 1903.\n- Rudolf Abel was a Soviet intelligence officer.\n- In 1960, Francis Gary Powers was a U.S. Air Force pilot whose U-2 spy plane was shot down over the Soviet Union.\n- During the Cold War, James B. Donovan represented Rudolf Abel, a convicted Soviet KGB spy held by the United States, at trial.\n- During the Cold War, James B. Donovan was entrusted with negotiating the release of Francis Gary Powers in exchange for Rudolf Abel.\n- Bridge of Spies tells the story of James B. Donovan and this spy exchange.\n- Rudolf Abel died on November 15, 1971.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
